- New sponsor has come forward to fund the CARL 7 wifi controlled coding robot
- Nov 2018 an online live google document was created for all to add best practices
- Sept 2018 two local parts companies will be offering CARL 6.1 parts    (see  buy link)
- Sept our open source robot is open to anyone to build, we can provide links to our parts manufacturers
- Sept 2018 our parts are in, registration is open
- Thanks to 3d modeling from Design lst engineers,  we are rolling out  build you robot game this Sept , link soon
- New easy to use, short video clips are in the works ,   stay tuned
- Carleton University will be open to hosting day workshops for Teachers and the CARL 6.1 coding robot
- 24 Ottawa Engineers are in schools using the CARL 6.1 as part of their outreach program
- Wed night CARL 6.1 robot bootcamp are available for teachers at Maker Space North in Ottawa from 6 to 8pm    [(register for meetup)](https://www.meetup.com/Makerspace-North-Makers-Meetup/events/250048629/)
- 2018 we secured funding to provide CARL 6.1 robots to 300 Ottawa schools
- 65 new schools have registered for the Sept 2018 rollout of the CARL 6.1
- Faculty of Education at University of Ottawa used the CARL 6.1 during the summer coding institute.
- 2018  over 300 students coded the robots, thanks to 47 innovated teachers across Canada.
- 2017 Community stakeholders came together to form a program that would offer robots to schools with Teacher Librarians, who encouraged and empowered students to code the robot regardless of what subject they were enrolled in ([see list of partners](/thanks))
- 2017 St Peter partnered with Carleton University Faculty of engineering and design & Capital Robot to create a slimmer, easier to use, low cost, coding robot. CARL 6.1 was created.
- 2017 CARL 6 was shared with area schools.    CARL   Coding. Autonomous. Robotic. Learning system.
- 2017  Teacher partners and CGEP in Quebec develop a simple robot for coding exercises .   CARL 6 was created .
- 2017  CARL 5 is more about designing, and building, we now wanted a more coding robot
- 2016 Carlrobotics.com was created to be a support for the CARL 5 educational system
- 2016 the CARL 5 robot was created to allow students to design, built a line following robot.
- 2016 the TEJ class, designed the CARL 3,4, 5 robot systems that was used for some outreach at Carleton.
- 2015  Carleton University Faculty of engineering and design funds many Ottawa school robotic projects, one was the creation of the computer engineering course TEJ3M at St Peter high school
